    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0955" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg859"/>

                <head>No. 383.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1879-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 10, 1879</date>. (Received March 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In the dispatch No. 304, of this date, on
                    the financial affairs of this country, I refer to a law to impose an extra tax
                    on commerce. The object of the impost is to create a special fund for the
                    amortization of the treasury notes.</p>
                <p>As this law will to some degree affect our commerce, I inclose copy of the law in
                    the original Spanish, and a translation taken from the South Pacific Times of
                    Callao of the 8th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RICHARD GIBBS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d412-a1.xml" xpointer="d412-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
